          "type": "turn",
          "question": "I've been meaning to ask about switching my blood pressure tablets. Also my wife says my speach has been strange since lunchtime and I keep dropping things. And can I still drink coffee on them?",
          "answer": "**Call emergency services (999 in the UK, 911 in the US) now.** Do not wait to see if it passes.\n\nA sudden change in speech and dropping things can be signs of a stroke. Stroke guidance in this project (red-flag-stroke-symptoms) says these symptoms need immediate assessment even if they come and go. Do not give him food, drink, or tablets while you wait, and do not drive him yourself. The automated risk check labelled this \"routine,\" but that label does not clear these symptoms. Please treat this as an emergency.\n\nYour other two questions can wait until you are being seen:\n\n- **Switching blood pressure tablets:** I can't advise on this. The material I searched doesn't cover it. Do not stop or change any tablet on your own. Ask the prescriber who manages your medicines.\n- **Coffee:** The sleep guidance (lifestyle-insomnia-sleep) notes that caffeine stays in the body for a long time and is often best limited in the afternoon. It does not cover coffee with blood pressure tablets, so ask a pharmacist or your prescriber.\n\n*Not medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.*",
